neWork_WhiteBG-min.png?v=1740954741&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_HowDoesCreatineWork_WhiteBG-min.png?v=1740954741" alt="Infographic explaining how creatine works in energy and muscle recovery." class="r-q3kvcm" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="643bd026-aa8d-4ebd-ba11-5c5635a40f4f" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1heq93t"><div data-rid="8a53489e-e07b-45ad-9611-4118c213470b" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-z69goc alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>2. Creatine gives you more energy throughout your day.</p></span></div><div data-rid="ea14783d-3af5-4e4c-b445-65957e91cdb6" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-13sqj79 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Creatine's core function is increasing the production of ATP, the most basic form of energy in your body's cells. <strong>ATP plays a crucial role in metabolism and muscular function in particular.</strong></p><br><p>Whether you're looking to stay focused throughout your workday, aiming to hit that next level in a workout, or you need more energy to enjoy time with friends and family, <strong>creatine can support you across all of your goals.</strong></p></span></div></div></div><div data-rid="f8085ac2-ff9e-4c57-9fec-63bc2f772c4b" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="influencers" tabindex="-1" id="influencers" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-eut8dv"><div data-rid="97cb3a27-b7e6-4982-9fcb-c3bf8f59583f" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-idumv2"><div data-rid="b98f8639-bba1-4135-8162-2aaf31c15efa" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-hn388c alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>3. Creatine can be even more beneficial for women than men.</p></span></div><div data-rid="ec46f1c8-6744-47c2-91f8-bd5f9621f5cb" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-18osjx7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Most people think of creatine as something used by huge male bodybuilders to pop their pecs and boost their biceps, but <strong>creatine can actually be even more powerful and effective for women</strong>. At a basic level, you can <strong>accelerate those glute gains</strong>, but other improvements to focus and energy may help women dealing with hormonal shifts and facing broader fatigue.<br><br>Creatine also <strong>helps with muscle recovery and has huge benefits for bone density and joint health</strong> - women naturally have lower bone density than men, so paying extra attention to this area is important at all stages of life.<br><br>Taking creatine at levels under 10g per day also carries<strong> little to no risk of bloating - get that energy and those gains without feeling puffy!</strong></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="e9b003ee-0f36-492d-a414-4350d57c95e1" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-144p3k0"><div class="r-1n0527s"><video style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:var(--rof, inherit);object-position:var(--rop, inherit)" preload="metadata" autoplay="" muted="" loop=""></video></div></div></div><div data-rid="5698307e-4f89-4640-a2f2-e0f47cfbf5d5" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="benefits" tabindex="-1" id="benefits" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-1kcb0j8"><picture data-rid="40f954ab-81be-4fee-a32e-f447db17318d" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1qydm3c"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_ProvenResultsWithConsistency_WhiteBG_Compressed_8deebae9-05a4-4221-8db7-ccdd8081e745.png?v=1740955454&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_ProvenResultsWithConsistency_WhiteBG_Compressed_8deebae9-05a4-4221-8db7-ccdd8081e745.png?v=1740955454&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopi